## What to do
Port the geocoding tool from taina-v3-2 as a standalone module. This tool converts text location descriptions to GPS coordinates using OpenStreetMap Nominatim API.

**Export a function (NOT a Vercel AI SDK tool — just a plain async function):**

```typescript
export interface GeocodeResult {
  success: true;
  latitude: number;
  longitude: number;
  formattedAddress: string;
  locality?: string;
  country?: string;
  countryCode?: string;
  stateProvince?: string;
}

export interface GeocodeError {
  success: false;
  error: string;
}

export type GeocodeResponse = GeocodeResult | GeocodeError;

export async function geocodeLocation(query: string, countryCode?: string): Promise<GeocodeResponse>
```

**Behavior:**
- Calls `https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search` with params: `q`, `format=json`, `limit=1`, `addressdetails=1`
- If countryCode provided, adds `countrycodes` param (lowercased)
- Sets `User-Agent: Pi-Taina/1.0 (biodiversity-bot)`
- Parses first result: extracts lat/lon as numbers, display_name, address components
- Returns GeocodeResult on success, GeocodeError on failure (no results, network error, non-200 status)
- Handles: empty results array, fetch errors, non-200 responses

## Dont
- Do NOT use the Vercel AI SDK `tool()` wrapper — this is a plain function
- Do NOT import from taina-v3-2 — rewrite from scratch using the same Nominatim API
- Do NOT add rate limiting (Nominatim has its own)

