## What to do
Create a species identification function that analyzes a photo using Google Gemini (vision-capable). This is ported from taina-v3-2 but adapted for Gemini instead of Claude.

**Export:**

```typescript
export interface ImageQuality {
  overall: "excellent" | "good" | "fair" | "poor";
  sharpness: "sharp" | "slightly_blurry" | "blurry";
  distance: "close_up" | "medium" | "far" | "too_far";
  lighting: "good" | "acceptable" | "poor";
  keyFeaturesVisible: string[];
  keyFeaturesMissing: string[];
  suggestions: string[];
  suitableForPublication: boolean;
}

export interface SpeciesIdentification {
  commonName: string;
  scientificName: string;
  taxonomy: {
    kingdom: string;
    phylum: string;
    class: string;
    order: string;
    family: string;
  };
  confidence: "high" | "medium" | "low";
  conservationStatus: string;
  nativeRegions: string[];
  habitat: string;
  description: string;
  ecologicalRole: string;
  possibleAlternatives: string[];
  organismGroup: "plant" | "fungus" | "bird" | "mammal" | "insect" | "reptile" | "amphibian" | "marine" | "other";
  recommendedPhotos: string[];
  imageQuality: ImageQuality;
}

export interface IdentificationError {
  error: string;
  suggestion?: string;
}

export type IdentificationResult = SpeciesIdentification | IdentificationError;

// imageData: base64-encoded image data
// mimeType: e.g. "image/jpeg"
// userContext: optional notes from user (location, habitat, behavior)
// apiKey: Gemini API key
// model: Gemini model ID (default from EnvConfig.speciesIdModel)
export async function identifySpecies(
  imageData: string,
  mimeType: string,
  apiKey: string,
  model?: string,
  userContext?: string
): Promise<IdentificationResult>
```

**Behavior:**
- Uses `@google/generative-ai` SDK (Google Generative AI for Node.js)
- Creates `GoogleGenerativeAI` client with the provided apiKey
- Uses model from parameter, defaulting to `"gemini-2.5-flash"`
- Sends the image as inline_data (base64 + mimeType) along with the identification prompt
- Set `responseMimeType: "application/json"` in generationConfig to get structured JSON output
- The identification prompt should request JSON output with all fields from SpeciesIdentification
- Include the full organism-group-specific image quality evaluation instructions from taina-v3-2 (plants, birds, insects, fungi, reptiles, marine)
- Parse the JSON response, return typed result
- On JSON parse failure: return { commonName: "Unknown", scientificName: "Unknown", confidence: "low", description: rawText, ... } with defaults
- On API error: return { error: "Failed to analyze image", suggestion: "Try a clearer photo" }

## Dont
- Do NOT use Anthropic SDK — use `@google/generative-ai`
- Do NOT use Vercel AI SDK
- Do NOT import from taina-v3-2
- Do NOT handle Telegram-specific logic (downloading photos etc) — that is handled by the caller
- Do NOT read process.env — accept apiKey and model as parameters

