## What to do
Create a function that publishes a Darwin Core occurrence record to the community ATProto PDS. Ported from taina-v3-2 but simplified for the community account model.

**Export:**

```typescript
export interface TelegramUser {
  id: number;           // Telegram user ID (stable, numeric)
  username?: string;    // @username (can change)
  displayName: string;  // First name + last name
}

export interface OccurrenceInput {
  scientificName: string;
  vernacularName?: string;
  basisOfRecord?: string; // default "HumanObservation"

  // Location (at least one of GPS or text required)
  decimalLatitude?: number;
  decimalLongitude?: number;
  coordinateUncertaintyInMeters?: number;
  locality?: string;
  country?: string;
  countryCode?: string;

  // Optional
  eventDate?: string;  // ISO 8601, defaults to today
  habitat?: string;
  behavior?: string;
  individualCount?: number;
  occurrenceRemarks?: string;

  // Image (raw bytes, will be uploaded to PDS as blob)
  imageData?: Buffer;
  imageMimeType?: string;

  // Who submitted this (Telegram user info)
  submittedBy: TelegramUser;
}

export interface PublishResult {
  success: true;
  uri: string;
  cid: string;
  scientificName: string;
  vernacularName?: string;
  location: string;
  date: string;
  hasImage: boolean;
}

export interface PublishError {
  success: false;
  error: string;
}

export type PublishResponse = PublishResult | PublishError;

export async function publishOccurrence(input: OccurrenceInput): Promise<PublishResponse>
```

**Behavior:**
- Calls `getAtprotoAgent()` from `../atproto.ts` to get the authenticated agent
- Validates: must have either GPS coords or text location, must have scientificName
- Builds record with `$type: "app.gainforest.dwc.occurrence"`
- Sets `recordedBy` to: `"{displayName} (@{username}, tg:{id})"` — all three Telegram user identifiers. If username is undefined, omit the @username part.
- Sets `recordedByID` to `"telegram:{id}"` 
- Sets `rightsHolder` to the community handle (from getCommunityHandle())
- If imageData provided: uploads to PDS via `agent.uploadBlob(imageData, { encoding: imageMimeType })`, attaches as `imageEvidence: [{ file: blobRef }]`
- Serializes blob ref through JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(blob)) to avoid CID serialization issues (same pattern as taina-v3-2)
- Publishes via `agent.com.atproto.repo.createRecord({ repo: did, collection: "app.gainforest.dwc.occurrence", record })`
- Sets `eventDate` to today if not provided
- Sets `createdAt` to ISO timestamp
- Sets `geodeticDatum: "EPSG:4326"` when GPS coords present
- Sets `occurrenceStatus: "present"`

## Dont
- Do NOT use OAuth — uses the community account from atproto.ts
- Do NOT accept image URLs — accept raw Buffer (the Telegram bot layer downloads the photo and passes bytes)
- Do NOT import from taina-v3-2
- Do NOT add multiple image support yet — single image is fine for MVP

