## What to do

### Problem
The `reply()` function defaults to `parseMode: "HTML"` (line 253), but the Pi agent outputs Markdown (`*bold*`, `- bullets`, etc.). Telegram's HTML mode ignores Markdown syntax, so formatting appears as raw asterisks and dashes.

### Fix in telegram.ts

1. Change the default `parseMode` from `"HTML"` to `"Markdown"` on line 253:
```typescript
const parseMode = options?.parseMode ?? "Markdown";
```

2. Add a fallback mechanism: if sending with Markdown fails (Telegram throws on malformed Markdown), retry without parse_mode. Wrap the `bot.api.sendMessage` call in a try/catch:
```typescript
try {
  await bot.api.sendMessage(chatId, chunks[i], {
    parse_mode: parseMode,
    reply_parameters: isFirst && options?.replyToMessageId !== undefined
      ? { message_id: options.replyToMessageId }
      : undefined,
  });
} catch (err) {
  // Markdown parsing failed — send as plain text
  console.warn("Failed to send with parse_mode, retrying as plain text:", err instanceof Error ? err.message : err);
  await bot.api.sendMessage(chatId, chunks[i], {
    reply_parameters: isFirst && options?.replyToMessageId !== undefined
      ? { message_id: options.replyToMessageId }
      : undefined,
  });
}
```

### No changes to index.ts
The callers in index.ts don't pass parseMode, so they'll pick up the new default automatically.

## Don't
- Don't use MarkdownV2 — it requires escaping special characters which the agent doesn't do
- Don't modify the sendPhoto function
- Don't change the splitMessage function
- Don't add any dependencies

